systemd: fall back to SIGCHLD/waitid when the kernel has no pidfd

sd_event_add_child() calls pidfd_open() and returns -ENOSYS on a kernel older
than 5.3, with no fallback.  systemd-udevd registers every worker that way, so on
dandelion's 4.9.190 udevd spawned 34 workers, could not watch any of them, and
processed zero events: /run/udev/data and /run/udev/links were never created, the
workers piled up as zombies and stage-1's 'udevadm settle' blocked forever.
Measured on hardware, attempt 14.

sd-event still carries the SIGCHLD path for the non-WEXITED case, so the fallback
is mostly a matter of not insisting on the pidfd: EVENT_SOURCE_WATCH_PIDFD() now
requires one, the four waitid(P_PIDFD) call sites go through child_waitid(), and
kill()/sigqueue() stand in for pidfd_send_signal().  pidref.c already handled
fd < 0 in every consumer; only pidref_set_pid() refused to construct such a PidRef.

This loses what the pidfd guarantees -- the pid is no longer pinned, so pid reuse
is racy again.  That is the pre-5.3 status quo, and the alternative on this device
is no udev at all.

--- a/src/basic/pidref.c	2026-07-31 12:09:38.640949083 -0500
+++ b/src/basic/pidref.c	2026-07-31 12:10:47.719989001 -0500
@@ -106,8 +106,9 @@
 
         fd = pidfd_open(pid, 0);
         if (fd < 0) {
-                /* Graceful fallback in case the kernel is out of fds */
-                if (!ERRNO_IS_RESOURCE(errno))
+                /* Graceful fallback in case the kernel is out of fds, or predates pidfd_open()
+                 * altogether (Linux 5.3). Every consumer in this file already handles fd < 0. */
+                if (!ERRNO_IS_RESOURCE(errno) && !ERRNO_IS_NOT_SUPPORTED(errno))
                         return log_debug_errno(errno, "Failed to open pidfd for pid " PID_FMT ": %m", pid);
 
                 fd = -EBADF;
--- a/src/libsystemd/sd-event/sd-event.c	2026-07-31 12:09:38.594288432 -0500
+++ b/src/libsystemd/sd-event/sd-event.c	2026-07-31 12:10:35.752042233 -0500
@@ -51,9 +51,24 @@
         /* Returns true if this is a PID event source and can be implemented by watching EPOLLIN */
         return s &&
                 s->type == SOURCE_CHILD &&
+                s->child.pidfd >= 0 &&
                 (s->child.options & ~WNOWAIT) == WEXITED;
 }
 
+static int child_waitid(sd_event_source *s, siginfo_t *si, int flags) {
+        /* waitid(P_PIDFD) needs Linux 5.4 and pidfd_open() 5.3. On kernels without them
+         * sd_event_add_child() leaves child.pidfd unset, and the child is addressed by pid. */
+
+        assert(s);
+        assert(s->type == SOURCE_CHILD);
+
+        if (s->child.pidfd >= 0)
+                return waitid(P_PIDFD, s->child.pidfd, si, flags);
+
+        assert(s->child.pid > 0);
+        return waitid(P_PID, s->child.pid, si, flags);
+}
+
 static bool event_source_is_online(sd_event_source *s) {
         assert(s);
         return s->enabled != SD_EVENT_OFF && !s->ratelimited;
@@ -1098,10 +1113,12 @@
 
